Thanks for the PR @dalerazimov. I pushed an update that keeps the flush part and drops the deferred nack.

When the batch handler nacks while the message is dispatched, that dispatch fails. Outer middlewares can then undo what the next handlers did: `dispatch_after_current_bus` drops the messages they dispatched, and `doctrine_transaction` rolls back their queries. If we keep their handled stamps, a retry skips them and that work is lost. The worker should rather use the exception of the bus in this case, that's #67647.

@andreybolonin two batch handlers on the same message is a separate issue. The transport message is also acked twice there, so I'd keep it out of this PR.
